Karthik, Ishaan,

Two things. One is a design question for Karthik and one is a set of numbers I
want sanity checked before I put them into the wireframe notes.

Design question first. On the Product Mix page, the moment I put a slicer on
Category the page stops agreeing with the Primary Sales page. It is not a
measure problem, I rewrote the measure twice before I accepted that. The rows
sitting on PRODUCT_KEY = -1 carry UNKNOWN for brand, for category, for pack
size, for everything, so the moment you slice on any product attribute those
rows fall out of the visual and the total drops. Same dataset, same date range,
two different totals on two pages. That is the single worst thing you can put
in front of a user, because after that they stop believing both numbers and
not just the wrong one.

Options as I see them and I do not fully like any of them.

a. Show UNKNOWN as a real member in the slicer so the user can see it and
   include it. Honest. Ugly. Somebody will screenshot it and send it to
   Rajeev within a week.
b. Leave it out and put a footnote on the page saying roughly two percent of
   lines are not classified. Cleaner page. Nobody reads footnotes, and the
   people who do read them are not the people who need to.
c. Fix it upstream so the fact rows get re-pointed once the dimension row
   turns up, and then it stops being a reporting problem at all.

My preference is c with a as the interim, but c is not mine to decide. One
visual, one message, and at the moment this page is carrying two, na?

The numbers, from Meghna below. I have used these in the notes, correct me if
I have taken the wrong end of them:

- 2.0 percent of invoiced volume lands on PRODUCT_KEY = -1
- 8,140 lines a month on average
- 11,902 in Jan-2026, which is the peak
- DQ-R-04 sitting at 98.0 percent against a 99.5 percent threshold

Karthik, straight question and a straight answer is fine even if the answer is
no. Is late arriving dimension handling inside the remediation build or is it
not? If it is not going in before UAT I will build option a now and we live
with it. What I do not want to do is build a, throw it away, and then rebuild
the page halfway through UAT with testers watching.

Priya's point below is the one I would actually put in front of the sponsor,
not mine. Mine is a layout problem. Hers is a trust problem, and hers is worse.

Screenshots of both pages are in the DEV folder, I have not attached them here,
the mail gets too big and then it bounces.

Ritwik

